Source: lys-login
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Build-Depends:
 debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://github.com/stubbedev/lys-login
Vcs-Git: https://github.com/stubbedev/lys-login.git
Vcs-Browser: https://github.com/stubbedev/lys-login

Package: lys-login
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 libpam0g,
 libpam-systemd,
 systemd
Recommends:
 lys-wm,
 lys-secrets,
 libvulkan1,
 mesa-vulkan-drivers
Provides: x-display-manager
Description: display manager, greeter and lock screen for the lys desktop
 lys-login is the lys desktop's login screen: the greeter, the session
 lock lys-shell starts, and a display manager of its own that shows the
 greeter in a lys-wm kiosk and starts the session through PAM.
 .
 The package enables nothing: switch to it with
 systemctl enable lys-login after disabling the current display manager.
 It installs the lys-login PAM service the display manager logs in
 through and the lys-shell PAM service the lock screen unlocks with.
